  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in your EUR account (ACC-1005). The amount is **EUR 240.00**, and the details are:\n\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Type:** Card payment, outgoing\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nThere is also another transaction, TX-0402, for **EUR 240.00** to the same merchant on 2026-07-14. You may want to check whether that is related.\n\nThese reason codes could apply, depending on what happened:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge**: You were charged more than once for the same purchase. This could fit if TX-0402 is a second charge for the same order as TX-0401.\n2. **unauthorized_debit**: You did not authorize the payment.\n3. **fraud_card_not_present**: The payment was made online without your card being present, and it was fraudulent. This fits an online merchant charge you did not make.\n4. **goods_not_received**: You paid for something you never received.\n5. **service_not_rendered**: You paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nWhich of these fits depends on the facts. If you tell me what happened, I can check whether a dispute is eligible under the matching code before anything is filed. I will not open a dispute without your confirmation.",
